<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  INERT TEMPLATE. Not referenced by CMakeLists.txt or any workflow. See README.md.

  Entitlements for WAMThumbnail.appex. This file contains exactly the one
  entitlement the 2026-08-23 experiment proved is REQUIRED, and nothing else.

  PROVEN REQUIRED
    com.apple.security.app-sandbox
      Without it, pluginkit refuses to register the appex at all -- the
      extension never appears and Finder keeps the generic icon. This is not a
      runtime failure you can debug from the provider; registration simply
      never happens.

  PROVEN *NOT* REQUIRED -- deliberately absent
    com.apple.security.files.user-selected.read-only
      QuickLook hands the extension a read-only sandbox extension for the
      specific QLFileThumbnailRequest.fileURL. Verified: open(O_RDONLY) plus
      pread at offset 0 AND at (size - 1024) on a 90 MB .mkv all succeeded with
      app-sandbox alone. Whole-file random access -- including the Cues at EOF
      that the demuxer needs -- works without any file-access entitlement.

  NOT NEEDED
    No network, no camera/microphone, no user-selected read-write, no
    security-scoped bookmarks. The provider reads one file it is handed and
    returns pixels.

  MUST NOT APPEAR
    com.apple.security.get-task-allow -- scripts/bundle_macos_lib.zsh:1658-1663
    and scripts/release_macos_notarize.zsh:309-329 both hard-fail the release
    if any packaged binary carries it.

  UNVERIFIED
    The experiment signed ad-hoc WITHOUT hardened runtime. Release mode adds
    --options runtime (scripts/bundle_macos_lib.zsh:1692). Sandbox + hardened
    runtime + Developer ID is an untested combination -- re-verify before
    shipping. Note also that the signing loop currently applies one flat
    argument array to every leaf (:1690-1695) and has no per-target
    entitlements hook, so wiring this file up requires a branch there.
-->
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.app-sandbox</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
